<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis Nicholson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1655">1655</a>–<a href="/years/1728">1728</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis Nicholson was an English army officer and colonial administrator who governed several American colonies. As lieutenant governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-andros">Sir Edmund Andros</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a>, he was driven out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leislers-rebellion">Leisler's Rebellion</a> in 1689. He later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, where he moved the capital to Williamsburg, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>.</p></div>
